Z||000000||Roy||08-19-99||03:18 PM||||Im looking for the best brand of touchup paint, also what is the best kind to use? I have a few minor nicks on my new paintjob and I just want to touch them up so water doesn't get under the paint.
Z||000001||Cooter||08-19-99||04:37 PM||||If the paint is new, ask the shop who did the paint if they will give (or sell) you some of the paint leftover from the paint job. I usually have about a pint of mixed paint leftover from an overall paint job that I keep for about a year so if any is needed for touch up, I give the customer some. I dont give it up front because most people dont keep up with it or it goes bad because it freezes in the tool shed.
Z||000002||Formula||08-19-99||04:46 PM||||you don't want rust. (snicker)
